  "biobricks:reviewNotes": "Determined by the BioBricks licensing-annotation agent (Claude). The brick is a direct parquet conversion of the NCBI dbSNP latest_release VCF pulled from the open NCBI FTP. dbSNP is produced by/for the US government (NCBI/NIH); NCBI content is public domain and NCBI places no restrictions on use or redistribution => open / permitted, with attribution to NCBI/dbSNP requested. HUMAN REVIEWER: note NCBI's standard caveat that individual original variant submitters may in principle claim IP rights, though dbSNP aggregate variation data is treated as public domain in practice.",
